    {
      "id": "claim_04a81b7419d245f3bdf24ed3ac750ef5",
      "statement": "The OpenWiki update workflow serializes itself with `concurrency: openwiki-update` and `cancel-in-progress: true` so that a manual run and the schedule cannot split the baseline commit, and checks out full history (`fetch-depth: 0`) because `openwiki code --update` diffs HEAD against the commit it last documented and a shallow clone hides that commit, producing an empty change summary.",
